WEBVTT

00:00:28.454 --> 00:00:30.288
produce new neurons,

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:34.162
the microscopic units
that make up the brain's tissue.

00:00:34.246 --> 00:00:38.079
Those newly generated neurons migrate
to various parts of the developing brain,

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:42.079
making it self-organize
into different structures.

00:00:43.121 --> 00:00:44.454
But until recently,

00:00:44.496 --> 00:00:49.996
scientists thought cell production came to
an abrupt halt after this initial growth,

00:00:50.037 --> 00:00:53.037
leading them to conclude
that neurological diseases,

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:55.162
such as Alzheimer’s and Parkinson’s,

00:00:55.204 --> 00:00:59.496
and damaging events
such as strokes, are irreversible.

00:00:59.871 --> 00:01:01.912
But a series of recent discoveries